jotain NEWS                                               -*- outline -*-

User-visible changes worth mentioning, newest first, after the GNU
Coding Standards (NEWS File).  jotain has no releases, so changes are
grouped by year; CHANGELOG.md lists them in detail.

* Noteworthy changes in 2026

** New features

  Pull request review: C-x p V (repo-review-pullreq) opens a Forge pull
  request or merge request as read-only diffs.  Draft comments are saved
  with c and posted with P after a confirmation, files are marked viewed
  with v, and optional gptel commands draft and check review comments.

  Per-user installs: services.jotain.users.<name> in the NixOS module
  installs the wrapped Emacs, the EDITOR and VISUAL scripts and jotctl
  in a user's profile.

  Kotlin: Eglot starts kotlin-lsp or kotlin-language-server, ktfmt
  formats on save, ktlint and detekt report through Flymake, and dape
  debugs through kotlin-debug-adapter.  C-c C-t runs Gradle tests and
  C-c C-z opens a REPL.  All tools come from the project PATH.

  More language modes: KDL, jq, GLSL, Gherkin, MDX, JSONC and
  build.zig.zon files.  Man pages get Flymake diagnostics from mandoc.

  Merge tools: C-c ^ S in smerge-mode re-resolves a conflicted file with
  mergiraf, and jotain-magit-delta-enable renders magit diffs through
  delta.

  Dev shell: nix develop (or nix-shell) provides the tooling for this
  repository, including prek, convco and gitleaks for the commit hooks.

** Changes in behavior

  gptel defaults to the direct Claude backend (claude-sonnet-5-5,
  ANTHROPIC_API_KEY).  The OpenRouter backend stays selectable from the
  C-c S menu.

  The LikeC4 major mode is now jotain-likec4-mode.

  Open .h files as C, format Python with ruff and use lua-ts-mode for
  Lua.

  Commits follow Conventional Commits, checked by a convco commit-msg
  hook, with gitleaks scanning staged files.

** Removed features

  Darwin, aarch64-linux and the terminal-only build were dropped: the
  flake builds one pgtk Emacs for x86_64-linux.

  The nix-on-droid module, devenv and services.jotain.devenv.enable
  were removed.

** Bug fixes

  services.jotain.spell.dictionaries reaches jinx again: a non-empty
  list sets ASPELL_CONF in the wrapped Emacs.
